  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="5371-3c33-498f-3e55" name="French Hundred Years War (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>HUNDRED YEARS WAR FRENCH 1337-1445 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.32-33). Keeper of the Oriflamme: if French armies are led by the King himself, the Oriflamme (Gold Flame) may be carried as the army battle standard (+50 pts). It may only be accompanied by a unit of Knights or a Combined Formation of Knights and Esquires; that unit is immune to panic. If the unit surrenders the Oriflamme to a victorious opponent it is worth 250 Victory points; its powers are lost when the Battle Standard Bearer is killed. Arrogant Pride: if a unit containing French Knights and/or Esquires charges an enemy unit, any unit containing mounted French Knights and/or Esquires within 12" of the charging unit must charge its nearest enemy (or, if none is in charge distance, move at least 4" towards the nearest enemy within its charge arc).

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[French Hundred Years War]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 25-75%, Infantry 25-75%. Artillery: 0-1 guns per 1,000 army points, bought from the Infantry allocation. Allies: 0-25% from the Scotland and the Borders list (documented only).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
